{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "e9b8f7a0-6a3b-4b1e-9b0e-3d7c2a6f4c2d",
    "name": "RH Demo - Scenario bout en bout (MySQL -> Airbyte -> PostgreSQL -> API)",
    "description": "Rejoue tests/scenario_bout_en_bout.md : chaine MySQL (source) -> Airbyte (replication) -> PostgreSQL (cible) -> API Flask (lecture seule). Suivre les dossiers dans l'ordre 0 a 6 pendant la demo.\n\nVariables a verifier avant de lancer (Collection > Variables) :\n- base_url, airbyte_url : adapter si les ports/hotes changent.\n- airbyte_client_id / airbyte_client_secret : donnes par `abctl local credentials`.\n- airbyte_connection_id : id de la connexion `rh_source_to_rh_target` (donne par `configure_airbyte.py`).\n- matricule : employe utilise pour la demo (EMP0001 par defaut).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "http://localhost:5000/api/v1", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "airbyte_url", "value": "http://localhost:8000", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "airbyte_client_id", "value": "9609b315-291a-4822-8098-7aeb1577575e", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "airbyte_client_secret", "value": "gNpYoSSj1xR7M3qdfRNPVyeUPV3lsZZx", "type": "secret" },
    { "key": "airbyte_connection_id", "value": "c3af8f86-0726-4dea-abd9-4bb902481cb7", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "airbyte_token", "value": "", "type": "secret" },
    { "key": "airbyte_job_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "matricule", "value": "EMP0001", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Sante",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/health", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["health"] }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"status = ok\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql(\"ok\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Donnees presentes apres synchronisation initiale",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /employes/{{matricule}}",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/employes/{{matricule}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["employes", "{{matricule}}"]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"a les champs attendus\", () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.all.keys('matricule','nom','prenom','email','date_embauche','actif','updated_at','service_code','service_nom','fonction_code','fonction_libelle');",
                  "});",
                  "console.log('nom actuel =', body.nom, '| service =', body.service_code, '| fonction =', body.fonction_code);",
                  "console.log('Attendu avant toute modification (etape 3) : nom=KABORE, service_code=DSI, fonction_code=DEV');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Recherche par matricule, service, fonction",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /employes?matricule=EMP00",
          "request": {
